# The search says where the outer loop stores into the list that is searched. With selects for low and high each load would wait for the comparison before it, and each
# search for the store before it, so nothing would overlap: 40 numbers nearly in order took twice the cycles. The branch stays.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="insertByBinarySearch" role=Source
# CHECK-NOT: Select(
# CHECK-LABEL: name="insertByBinarySearch" role=GenericVersion
# A search that stores nowhere keeps its selects: one search does not wait for another, and keys in no order are found in under half the cycles.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="placeOf" role=Source
# CHECK-COUNT-2: Select(
# CHECK-NOT: Select(
